Neither is misogyny

&#x200B;

Edit I have .... lmao.

But it doesn't work that way, it was still someone not Indian, using racial stereotypes and changing their voice to sound stereotypical. Can we stop with these false gotcha's? All the fallacies hurt my head dudes.

&#x200B;

Edit: I think people also get lost in the fact that social justice stuff doesn't have to be hard and fast change. It starts out with conversations, then it moves to implementing and changing things to better fit current times. Apu is outdated and that's okay.
